  "cn": "第 20 集 · 奇迹",
  "novel": "After a [[taxi|taxi]] [[accident|accident]], Ted [[believed|believe]] in [[miracles|miracle]]. \"We [[survived|survive]],\" he [[whispered|whisper]]. \"That's a miracle.\"\n\nBarney tried to [[debunk|debunk]] the idea. \"There are no miracles,\" he [[declared|declare]]. \"Only [[statistics|statistics]] and [[luck|luck]].\"\n\nBut Barney himself was in a [[near-death|near-death]] experience. A bus had nearly hit him. He walked away [[unscathed|unscathed]]. For one [[brief|brief]] moment, even Barney [[wondered|wonder]].\n\nMarshall and Lily felt [[grateful|grateful]] for every moment. Robin [[realized|realize]] how much Ted [[meant|mean]] to her. The group gathered at MacLaren's, [[closer|close]] than ever.\n\n\"Maybe miracles aren't about [[surviving|survive]],\" Ted said, [[raising|raise]] his glass. \"Maybe they're about the people who are still here.\"\n\nBarney [[rolled|roll]] his eyes. But he clinked his glass anyway. Friendship, Ted [[realized|realize]], was the real [[miracle|miracle]].",
